## 1. Permission to View and Modify

The source code of One-Block Reborn may be publicly viewed, studied, modified,
rewritten, and adapted for another Minecraft, NeoForge, or compatible version.

You may:

- view and study the source code;
- modify the source code;
- rewrite or adapt the source code for another version;
- create private modified versions;
- use modified versions privately;
- share a modified version inside your own private/local circle of friends.

## 2. Modified Versions May Not Be Publicly Distributed

A modified version of One-Block Reborn may **not be publicly distributed** while
the original One-Block Reborn project is actively maintained.

This includes publishing or uploading a modified version for public download,
publishing it on mod platforms, releasing it as a separate public mod, selling
it, or including it in a publicly distributed modpack.

Private use and sharing within a local circle of friends are permitted.

## 3. Original Authorship

Modifying or adapting the source code does not transfer authorship of the
original One-Block Reborn project.

You may credit yourself for your own changes, but you may not claim to be the
original creator of One-Block Reborn or remove the original author's attribution.

## 4. Twelve-Month Inactivity Rule

If the original One-Block Reborn project has received no official update,
release, or meaningful development activity for a continuous period of at least
twelve (12) months, public distribution of modified versions becomes permitted.

The twelve-month period is measured from the most recent official update,
release, or meaningful development activity of the original project.

## 5. Attribution When Public Distribution Becomes Permitted

A modified version publicly distributed under Section 4 must clearly credit the
original creator and identify the original One-Block Reborn project.

At minimum, the distributor must include:

**Original Project:** One-Block Reborn
**Original Author:** _sn0w1_
**Original Repository:** the official One-Block Reborn repository

The distributor may additionally credit themselves for their own modifications,
but may not claim to be the original creator of One-Block Reborn.

## 6. License Preservation

This license must remain included with any publicly distributed modified version
permitted under Section 4. The original author's attribution must not be removed.

## 7. Commercial Use

Commercial distribution or sale of One-Block Reborn, including modified versions,
is not permitted without explicit written permission from the original author.

## 8. No Warranty

One-Block Reborn is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied. The original author is not responsible for damage, data loss, server
problems, incompatibilities, or other issues resulting from use or modification.

## 9. License Changes

The original author may change or replace this license for future versions.
The license included with a particular released version applies to that version,
subject to applicable law.

## 10. Plain-Language Summary

**You may read, study, modify, rewrite, and privately use One-Block Reborn.**

